"Glowing golden ropes of magic chain Gorgon to the consulate desk, trailing like jellyfish."
"Living things cannot pass through the ropes, and his wrists are raw beneath them."
"The bindings let him reach every public area of the Chicago consulate."
"They bar him from telling humans what is not widely known of Artonans, the System or magic."
"They also bar talk of chaos, his own kind and extra-dimensional incursions."
"He cannot ask for food; it must be offered before he can take or refuse it."
"He may give directions, register classes, witness pre-affixation trades and hand out pens."
"He may not make contracts that invest anyone with his authority."
"Speaking past them costs him; one outburst was a costly moment of melancholy."
